spring: -2,-6 water
hub: -5,0 water
spring: -2,-3 wind
hub: 3,-3 wind
spring: -9,3 crystal
hub: -13,3 crystal

# Water wants bends, wind and crystal want straights. The counts are what the routes need plus slack,
# because a corridor with no spare tile is a corridor a single unlucky draw ends.
tile: 0,3 crystal x5
tile: 0,2 water x7
tile: 0,3 wind x6

# The board's own solution, replayed by the solvability gate rather than searched for. The search cannot
# finish on a board like this: what costs it is open space, and open space is what this biome is made of
# now — the routes are spines of islands rather than corridors, so almost every cell has somewhere legal
# to go.
#
# It reaches 578 against a target of 550 in 11 moves, spending 0 of its three skips.
#
# Rotations are written down. They are optional in the format, but on open ground several rotations join
# something legally at almost every cell and only one continues the route.

solve: -1,-3 rot 0
solve: -2,-5 rot 2
solve: -3,-4 rot 5
solve: 0,-3 rot 0
solve: 1,-3 rot 0
solve: 2,-3 rot 0
solve: -3,-2 rot 2
solve: -3,-3 rot 2
solve: -4,-2 rot 5
solve: -10,3 rot 0
solve: -4,-1 rot 2
